Summary:
In this session, we learned about backend architecture using Express and the importance of organizing backend projects using the MVC (Model-View-Controller) structure. The session began with a recap of previous topics such as React frontend basics, Node.js introduction, Express server setup, REST APIs, and middleware. We discussed the problems with writing all backend logic in a single file and how it becomes difficult to maintain as the project grows. The concept of MVC architecture was introduced, explaining the roles of routes, controllers, and models in handling API requests. The session also demonstrated a professional backend folder structure and how routes are connected to controllers and the server.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, we understood the importance of structured backend architecture in real-world applications. We learned how MVC architecture helps in organizing code, improving scalability, and making backend projects easier to manage. We also gained knowledge about separating responsibilities between routes and controllers and how requests flow through different layers in a backend application. This session helped us understand industry-standard backend development practices and how multiple developers can collaborate efficiently in a well-structured project.
